    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1120">

                <pb facs="1103" n="1091" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg1091"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94115 Exchange/10–1144: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-10-11">October 11,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received October 11—8:57 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6790. American Interests—Far East. Department’s 2565, July 26.<anchor n="70"
                        xml:id="d1120-f1"/> Foreign Office note October 9 states during interview at
                    Japanese Foreign Office Gorgé informed that Japanese do not believe possible
                    exchange at Soviet port, exchange via Siberia believed possible however, but
                    Japanese are of opinion Mormugão should be exchange port. Japanese Foreign
                    Office believes American-Japanese exchange should be deferred until conclusion
                    second Anglo-Japanese exchange <pb facs="1104" n="1092" xml:id="pg1092"/> which
                    appears more urgent but now encountering serious technical difficulties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1120-f1" n="70" xml:id="d1120-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed; it stated, “Since it requires approximately 45 days for the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gripsholm</hi> to reach Mormugão from New York,
                    preliminary arrangements should soon be begun if a further exchange of American
                    and Japanese nationals is to take place at that port as soon as the monsoon ends
                    in October.” (711.94115 Exchange/7–2644)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
